WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.376
Wukong stared at the cave door, shocked.

2
00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:07.754
[g@"I don't believe it.

3
00:00:07.755 --> 00:00:12.113
One-Horned Buffalo stole our weapons again!"@g]

4
00:00:12.114 --> 00:00:16.821
"What will we do now?" asked the fire god.

5
00:00:16.822 --> 00:00:21.939
"This demon's powers are stronger than any I've seen before," said Wukong.

6
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.657
[g@"I know one person who can definitely defeat him—Buddha.

7
00:00:26.658 --> 00:00:28.386
I'll be back soon."@g]

8
00:00:28.387 --> 00:00:34.389
The monkey leaped onto a cloud and soared toward the West.

9
00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:38.070
[g@He arrived at the Thunderclap Monastery.

10
00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:41.750
A guard at the gate stopped him.@g]

11
00:00:41.751 --> 00:00:45.253
"I need to ask Buddha for help," Wukong told the guard.

12
00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:48.400
"It's about the Tang Monk's journey."

13
00:00:48.401 --> 00:00:51.051
The guard waved the monkey through.

14
00:00:51.052 --> 00:00:55.580
Wukong entered the monastery and bowed before Buddha.

15
00:00:55.581 --> 00:00:59.766
"Greetings, Buddha," said the monkey. "I need—"

16
00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:01.690
[g@Buddha held up a hand.

17
00:01:01.691 --> 00:01:04.838
"I know why you're here, Wukong.@g]

18
00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:08.146
[g@I also know who the demon is.

19
00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:11.628
You must go to Laozi for help."@g]

20
00:01:11.629 --> 00:01:18.308
"Oh, okay," said the monkey, a bit surprised. "Thank you."

21
00:01:18.309 --> 00:01:21.360
Wukong flew toward Heaven.

22
00:01:21.361 --> 00:01:24.782
"Laozi doesn't like me much," thought the monkey.

23
00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:32.195
"He won't be happy to see me."

24
00:01:32.196 --> 00:01:36.487
When Wukong arrived at Laozi's house, the sage frowned.

25
00:01:36.488 --> 00:01:40.023
"What do you want, Wukong?" asked Laozi.

26
00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:42.970
"Buddha told me to come here," said Wukong.

27
00:01:42.971 --> 00:01:47.406
"The Tang Monk was captured by a demon called One-Horned Buffalo."

28
00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:50.485
"Oh dear!" said Laozi.

29
00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:53.072
"Do you know him?" asked the monkey.

30
00:01:53.073 --> 00:01:56.184
[g@Laozi nodded. "He's my green buffalo.

31
00:01:56.185 --> 00:01:59.271
I didn't realize he'd escaped."@g]

32
00:01:59.272 --> 00:02:03.273
"Well, he did," said Wukong, getting annoyed.

33
00:02:03.274 --> 00:02:06.958
[g@"And he's planning to eat the Tang Monk.

34
00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.713
Your buffalo also has a metal ring.@g]

35
00:02:09.714 --> 00:02:13.772
Every time we try to fight him, the ring sucks in our weapons!"

36
00:02:13.773 --> 00:02:15.779
Laozi held up his hands.

37
00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:22.798
"Okay, okay. I can capture the buffalo. Don't worry."

38
00:02:22.799 --> 00:02:27.027
The sage went into another room.

39
00:02:27.028 --> 00:02:36.120
When he came back, he was holding a fan. "Let's go."

40
00:02:36.121 --> 00:02:40.091
Wukong and Laozi returned to the mountain.

41
00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:45.090
"Buffalo!" shouted Laozi. "Get out here right now!"

42
00:02:45.091 --> 00:02:50.646
The door flew open, and One-Horned Buffalo stepped outside.

43
00:02:50.647 --> 00:02:54.140
His face fell when he saw Laozi.

44
00:02:54.141 --> 00:02:59.882
Laozi raised the fan and brought it down fast.

45
00:02:59.883 --> 00:03:05.218
A fierce wind nearly knocked over One-Horned Buffalo.

46
00:03:05.219 --> 00:03:11.230
The demon pulled off the metal ring and flung it at Laozi.

47
00:03:11.231 --> 00:03:16.213
The sage caught it and brought the fan down once more.

48
00:03:16.214 --> 00:03:22.061
The wind knocked over the demon, and he turned into a large, green buffalo.

49
00:03:22.062 --> 00:03:26.035
The buffalo stood up and snorted.

50
00:03:26.036 --> 00:03:30.657
Laozi tucked the fan and the ring into his robe.

51
00:03:30.658 --> 00:03:37.147
Then he climbed onto the buffalo and rode up into the sky.

52
00:03:37.148 --> 00:03:43.168
Wukong went into the cave, and the warrior and two gods followed.

53
00:03:43.169 --> 00:03:46.251
They soon found their weapons.

54
00:03:46.252 --> 00:03:50.331
"The gods and I will return to Heaven now," said the warrior.

55
00:03:50.332 --> 00:03:53.078
"Good luck with your journey, Wukong."

56
00:03:53.079 --> 00:03:57.170
"Thank you," said the monkey.

57
00:03:57.171 --> 00:04:01.658
Wukong found his companions deep in the cave.

58
00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:08.666
"What took you so long?" cried Bajie.

59
00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:11.285
[g@"I was busy fighting a demon,"

60
00:04:11.286 --> 00:04:14.430
said Wukong, untying the Tang Monk.@g]

61
00:04:14.431 --> 00:04:16.946
"Thank you, Wukong," said the monk.

62
00:04:16.947 --> 00:04:19.279
"You're welcome," said the monkey.

63
00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:25.112
"But next time I tell you to stay away from a place, please listen!"

64
00:04:25.113 --> 00:04:29.779
A few weeks later, the travelers arrived at a busy city.

65
00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:35.819
The streets were filled with people selling vegetables, spices, and other goods.

66
00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.557
An old woman was stirring a large pot of soup.

67
00:04:39.558 --> 00:04:42.938
Other food sizzled over fires.

68
00:04:42.939 --> 00:04:46.926
[g@Bajie breathed deep.

69
00:04:46.927 --> 00:04:51.690
"Ah! That smells wonderful!"@g]

70
00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:55.716
Suddenly a young woman rushed out of the crowd.

71
00:04:55.717 --> 00:04:58.230
[g@"The Tang Monk!" she cried.

72
00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.890
She threw her arms around the monk.@g]

73
00:05:00.891 --> 00:05:10.116
A fierce wind swirled, and a second later they were both gone!

